
# --- GOLDEN FIXTURE (see docs/guests/ubuntu.md) ---
# Ubuntu 4.10 Warty Warthog live CD. The vmstate lives in ubuntu.qcow2 (empty 1G
# carrier); the ISO is read-only. Disk + ISO + launcher are an atomic set.
# RETRONET GOLDEN, baked 2026-09-03 on /data/vms/sandbox/ubuntu-rn/bake (exact
# launcher device set INCLUDING the new rtl8139 on tap ubunturn0): VM_SIZE=307
# MiB, VM_CLOCK=00:11:25.966 (qemu-img snapshot -l). Restore-proven: killed by
# pidfile, relaunched with -loadvm golden -S, QMP cont, fb-wait --settle 4
# landed in 4.1s on the identical scene; the OSCAR session and the web plane
# BOTH survived the restore (HiveBot replied in-frame, Firefox loaded a second
# corpus page). Screen is 640x480 (XFree86 vesa, no DDC).
# See docs/lab/retronet/STATION-ubuntu.md and docs/lab/UBUNTU-WAVE.md.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_RESET_MONITOR=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/ubuntu/reset-hmp.sock
SH_FIXTURE_DESC="Ubuntu 4.10 live session as 'warty' on the 640x480 GNOME 2.8 desktop with the Gaim 1.0 Buddy List open and signed in as UIN 18300 (HiveBot and the retronet fleet listed by name); Firefox 0.9 closed, its globe on the top panel; screensaver off; absolute USB tablet and keyboard ready"
SH_BASE_BACKUP=/data/gallery-guests/Ubuntu/ubuntu.qcow2.bak-pre-rn
